# Project Architecture

## Directory Structure

```
src/
└── app/
    ├── app.ts              # Root — bootstraps the app
    ├── app.routes.ts       # Route definitions
    ├── app.config.ts       # Providers and app-wide config
    ├── app.html            # Root template
    ├── components/         # Shared reusable components
    ├── pages/              # Route-level page components
    ├── services/           # Angular services (providedIn: 'root')
    ├── models/             # TypeScript interfaces and types
    ├── guards/             # Route guards
    ├── pipes/              # Custom pipes
    ├── directives/         # Custom directives
    └── utils/              # Helper functions
```

## Component Conventions

### Naming

| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Component file | `kebab-case` | `user-profile.component.ts` |
| Component class | `PascalCase` | `UserProfileComponent` |
| Template file | Same as TS + `.html` | `user-profile.component.html` |
| Style file | Same as TS + `.scss` | `user-profile.component.scss` |
| Test file | Same as TS + `.spec.ts` | `user-profile.component.spec.ts` |

### Component Structure

```typescript
@Component({
  selector: 'app-user-profile',
  changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,
  imports: [...],
  templateUrl: './user-profile.component.html',
  styleUrl: './user-profile.component.scss',
})
export class UserProfileComponent {
  // 1. Inputs (public)
  // 2. Outputs
  // 3. Public properties
  // 4. Private properties (signals, state)
  // 5. Computed values (computed())
  // 6. Lifecycle hooks
  // 7. Public methods
  // 8. Private methods
}
```

## Service Conventions

- Place in `services/`
- Use `inject()` or `providedIn: 'root'`
- One service = one concern
- All HTTP calls go through services — never directly in components
- Services return Observables or Promises

## Model Conventions

- Place in `models/`
- Use TypeScript interfaces for plain data
- Use classes for DTOs with methods
- Export all from `models/index.ts`

## Routing Conventions

```typescript
// app.routes.ts
export const routes: Routes = [
  { path: '', loadComponent: () => import('./pages/home/home.component') },
  { path: 'users', loadComponent: () => import('./pages/users/users.component'), canActivate: [authGuard] },
];
```

## Code Organization

- **Smart (container) components** — fetch data, manage state
- **Dumb (presentational) components** — accept inputs, emit outputs
- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks (Angular signals-based) or services
- Keep business logic out of templates
- Keep API URLs in environment files
